{"cache_key uses hash(tuple(...)) which is non-deterministic across Python processes due to PYTHONHASHSEED randomization, reducing cache effectiveness and making invalidate_upsampling_cache unpredictable": 0.9314826130867004, "In error_upsampling.is_errors_query_for_error_upsampled_projects, accessing snuba_params.project_ids may raise AttributeError since SnubaParams may use 'projects' attribute instead": 0.34834566712379456, "_are_all_projects_error_upsampled takes project_ids: Sequence[int] but callers may pass Project model instances instead of ints, causing type mismatch when comparing against allowlist": 0.14639803767204285, "organization_events_stats has duplicated import blocks and a stray closing parenthesis that will cause a SyntaxError": 0.04509834200143814, "Cache key should include dataset name if eligibility is dataset dependent, or document why it doesn't": 0.35620102286338806, "transform_query_columns_for_error_upsampling returns 'upsampled_count() as count' but downstream consumers may expect different alias formats": 0.058263350278139114, "Possible code duplication in discover.function_converter around the toInt64/sum sample_weight block when inserting the new upsampled_count function": 0.09640529751777649, "invalidate_upsampling_cache is defined but never called when options change - need to wire an options change hook or document that it must be called manually": 0.48091837763786316, "Integration tests rely on specific sample_weight behavior mapping sample_rate to sample_weight in Snuba, making tests brittle": 0.12825609743595123, "Docstrings mention 'ALL projects are allowlisted and we're querying error events' but should also mention the dataset-dependent _should_apply_sample_weight_transform condition": 0.037769071757793427, "Missing explicit unit tests for caching behavior to ensure cache key stability": 0.7075257301330566}